    "summary": "I built four full bases in a straight row at q=0 to 3, r=0. They form two pairs: the bases at q=0 and q=1 are joined by a joint bolt, and so are the bases at q=2 and q=3. The only thing joining the two pairs is one double side connector across the seam between q=1 and q=2. Each seam takes just one connector, so one is all that fits there. I capped all the open faces with solid end caps. I left out the lockJoints step on purpose, because it would have bolted the seam between the pairs too, and the brief says that seam gets side connectors only. The final check found no rule issues and no mesh clashes. The build has 25 parts.",
